cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Which check stopped it? Evaluating egress defenses for LLM agents"
authors:
  - family-names: "Reddi"
    given-names: "Sai Gowtham"
year: 2026
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gowtham44831/reliable-tool-routing"
abstract: >
  A bounded laboratory evaluation of a pre-dispatch egress gateway for
  LLM tool calls: host filtering, bounded payload decoding, field-level
  authorization against permission records, and identity-bound task
  context — evaluated with a local planner (qwen3:14b) and a second
  planner (gpt-6.1-sol) under a frozen protocol, with per-call deciding-
  check attribution and independent receiver ground truth. Fictional
  data, mock receivers; a laboratory experience report, not an efficacy
  claim or a novel security mechanism.
date-released: 2026-10-20
